module gunbc.fleet.machine_lifecycle

// THE LIFECYCLE OF A FLEET MACHINE IS A SET OF TRANSITIONS, AND EACH ONE HAS A MODELED ROUTE (P13 of
// gunbc.plans.fleet_machine_authority; 2.5, O4).
//
// THE REWRITE THIS MODULE IS FOR. 2.5 says a fleet machine's life has five transitions -- rename, rebind
// after repair, reprovision, change participation, retire and replace -- and O4's completion condition is
// that EACH has a modeled route and NONE is a hand step. Before this module a transition existed only as
// its after-state: `next_name` was a field, a board swap was something A2's fold survived, retiring a
// machine was deleting rows by hand. Nothing carried the event itself, so nothing could say which step a
// route runs and which step a person does. The hand-step shape is not even NAMEABLE here: a leg
// (TransitionProducer) is an arm that names a real producer -- live today, or planned with the PR that
// lands it. There is no arm for "an operator runs a command", so a transition can only be modeled by
// citing the producers that realize it. A hand step is caught by not being expressible
// (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder: "stronger than catching a wrong state is making it
// unwritable").
//
// WHAT THIS MODULE OWNS, AND WHAT IT ONLY CALLS. The STATUS is derived, never stored: Registered for a
// registry row, Active once the machine is enrolled, Retired once it stands in the retirement ledger -- so
// "what state is this machine in" is an observation of three real producers, not a column someone sets to
// whatever they are about to do. The LEDGER is a transition's output (retired_ledger_with is its only
// mint), never a row typed beside a task. Every REFUSAL is the real producer's own refusal carried in the
// producer's own type: the rebind refuses with bind_unit_key's UnitKeyRefusalCause and with the physical
// binding admission's verdict, the participation change refuses with the enrollment admission's verdict,
// and a reissue is refused by this module's ledger before A1's roster admission is even reached.
// Re-implementing a refusal here would mint a second authority over it -- a model that passes while the
// producer would refuse is exactly the misleading value this plan removes.
//
// NOTHING IS APPLIED TO A LIVE MACHINE FROM HERE. An admission returns a typed effect (TransitionEffect)
// and the route that would realize it; no effect is emitted and no transport is run. Each leg's live
// realization is the mode or workflow the leg's producer names, and a leg is one of three arms and no
// other: a producer live in the corpus today (RealProducer), a producer a NAMED STEP OF THIS PLAN will
// land (PlannedProducer, which carries the plan document as its own resolvable citation alongside the
// future site), or no producer at all (UnmodeledLeg). The third arm is not a route that reads as modeled:
// `route_is_modeled` reads it and reports the route unmodeled, so an unowned step can never be counted as
// covered: a leg whose own pointer says "unowned" turning the population claim green is rung inflation
// (gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder: an inflated class never ranks for climbing). What a leg may NOT
// be is a hand step -- no arm of TransitionProducer expresses one. Citations are read back through
// std.annotation_reference's own segment tests, which is a SHAPE test and says so: it keeps a paraphrase out
// of a field that names a declaration, and it does not decide whether that declaration exists. Existence is a
// corpus question, claimed once per population against the declaration index by the witness
// (test.claim.fleet.machine_lifecycle_witness.every_real_route_citation_is_a_declaration_the_corpus_declares).
//
// WHO TAKES THIS UP, named rather than implied. This module is the model P13 owes; the changes that RUN its
// routes are the steps listed in `machine_lifecycle_consumer_steps` and claimed there one by one: P11.x
// retires each host, which mints the ledger through `retired_ledger_with` and consumes
// `retirement_artifacts` (its acceptance is each artifact's own consumer running green after the artifact is
// removed), and P12 accepts a new machine, which is where reprovision is exercised live -- P13's own scope
// line defers that exercise to P12. `machine_retirement_ledger` is `[]` for the honest reason: the fleet has
// no retired machine today and the only writer is P11.x. A witness that minted a fake retirement to look
// exercised would be the misleading value this plan exists to remove, so instead the ledger is admitted to
// empty, its mint is the only way in, and every read in this module is exercised against the fleet's real
// rows and receipts.

import std.types { Bool, List, NonEmptyStr, String }
